# The one variable this console reads.
#
# It is read on the SERVER only — in server components, never in the browser. It is deliberately
# not prefixed `NEXT_PUBLIC_` and deliberately absent from `next.config.ts`'s `env` block, because
# both of those inline a value into the client bundle and the broker's address is not something a
# visitor needs.
#
# Leave it UNSET and the console renders the committed fixtures in `frontend/fixtures/`. That is
# the normal state for the public demo: the screens are complete and honest without a backend, and
# every screen says on its face that it is reading fixtures rather than a measurement.
#
# Set it to the broker's origin — no trailing slash, no path — to read the live API instead.
# BROKER_API_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8000

# There is no token variable here on purpose. This console sends no credential, and nothing it
# renders is one. If the broker ever requires an API key, it belongs in a server-side variable
# added here alongside this note — never in anything the browser can read.
